+# Two real public-entry Vite compositions — runtime UNRUN
+
+FR-01/05/07/13/14/15/16; AC-01/22–27. New Stage B source only. No new workspace
+package/manifest/dependency is introduced. Vite is declared and resolved from the
+existing `apps/storybook` installation, **not a dependency on Storybook runtime**.
+Both HTML pages are actual independent entry points; neither imports a story/host.
+
+- `index.html` → `main.tsx`: styled server-page application with one stable real
+  shared D/C/P/source owner, actual useDataTable/DataTable, one public details
+  accessory/provider/shell, bound utility trigger, synthetic row/bulk actions,
+  custom numeric editor/operator registry, full EN/AR bundle, locale/theme controls
+  and actual manual resource responses/retry. Server query changes require clicking
+  Deliver known/unknown page. This is intentional transport control, not a hung or
+  fake response. A source input is not an accepted/native-output cache.
+- `headless.html` → `headless.tsx`: genuine useDataTable/native semantic table with
+  search Apply/draft Cancel, native eligible selection, selection Cancel, sorting,
+  paging and terminal access loss. No HeroUI/styled/Tailwind/CSS/Storybook import is
+  reachable in its authored source/type graph. Complete client input contains
+  off-page objects; it does not pretend they are missing. Actual emitted closure
+  and browser stylesheet checks are authored but UNRUN.
+
+The source/model owner stays stable across queries and presentation changes. The
+styled owner stays above its detail content; DataTable owns the sole shell. The
+headless draft has a real P purge participant. All app actions are labeled synthetic
+and update actual source/notice/C state, not permissions, network or backend success.
+Revocation is terminal; no same-owner restoration button exists. Original shared
+Stage A public source is unchanged and not independently runtime approved here.
+No reordering configuration is offered: required dragging/G-02 remains blocked.
+
+## Commands (FINAL authorized execution phase only; none run here)
+
+From the repository root, after main selects and produces current emitted entries:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build
+node apps/storybook/node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js --config apps/storybook/vite.examples.config.ts
+```
+
+The strict development port is `http://127.0.0.1:6572/` and `/headless.html`.
+Do not start the old Storybook app or modify its aliases. Multi-page build, separately:
+
+```sh
+node apps/storybook/node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build --config apps/storybook/vite.examples.config.ts
+node tests/workbench/wp11-examples/emitted-graph.mjs
+```
+
+Output stays under `tests/workbench/wp11-examples/.artifacts/vite-dist/`. The finite
+runtime mappings point to **public emitted dist exports**, never library source.
+React/ReactDOM/scoped UI vendor resolution uses the actual declaring-app installation.
+Strict fs allowlists cover only examples, emitted packages and installed dependencies;
+credentials/Git/reference metadata are denied. No arbitrary system path is served.
+This emitted-workspace setup is NOT outside-workspace archive/ordinary-consumer proof.
+
+Only the new positive TS6/noEmit programs/static/scope/syntax/full Biome are allowed
+now; see `tests/workbench/wp11-examples/README.md` for exact evidence and deferred
+drivers. No app/module/browser/SSR/server/build has executed. No hardware/AT/visual,
+real consumer, packed/ordinary compatibility, full WP-11 or publication approval.
